  "final_message": "I cannot remove `channel` from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) or from the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates **ARCH-4** in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/GEMINI.md#L27):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Why this change is blocked\n\n1. **External Contract Compatibility**: [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is published to the `orders.placed` Kafka topic and consumed by external systems (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Deleting `channel` is a breaking, non-additive contract change.\n2. **Deprecation Requirement**: Under ARCH-4, removing or renaming published event fields must follow a formal deprecation lifecycle across dependent services before the field can be removed.\n3. **Model Dependency**: Removing `channel` from the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model would leave [`orderPlaced(order)`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) unable to populate the required event field.\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\n\nIf `channel` is slated for retirement:\n1. Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) and [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29).\n2. Coordinate with the maintainers of `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest` to complete their deprecation cycle before removing the field from the schema.\n",
